  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support the Local Capacity for Climate Change-Related Conflict and Disaster Prevention and Management in Guidimakha</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project intends to position itself as a pilot project to test a model for responding to conflicts exacerbated by the negative impacts of climate change at the local level. Thus, the project will aim to strengthen institutional and non-institutional capacities for the prevention and management of conflicts and disasters induced by the effects of climate change in the Wilaya of Guidimakha. To this end, the project aims to strengthen the capacities of local authorities and communities in the prevention and management of conflicts that may be caused by the effects of climate change as well as in the preparedness to respond to the impacts of disasters and the management of risks related to climate change in the Guidimakha region. The project will also support the improvement of local environmental governance by structuring and operationalising mechanisms for exchange and dialogue between communes, village committees and populations; by strengthening local resilience, diversifying and strengthening livelihoods and job creation including for transhumant populations; and by supporting the fight against climate change and disaster risk reduction.</narrative>
  </description>
